      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Florida State Road 59 cuts through Wacissa, leading just four miles north to U.S. Route 27 and connecting the community to Tallahassee and Monticello.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12,
        13,
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wacissa%2C_Florida",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "route_only"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Wacissa River’s narrow, swift channel is home to river otters, hawks, and a chorus of wading birds that sing amid cypress‑gum swamps.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25,
        28,
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.jeffersoncountyfl.gov/p/recreation-tourism",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Jefferson County’s Heritage Road System includes the Spanish Trace Trail, a color‑coded route that winds through historic sites and scenic towns like Wacissa.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
